Expose an opt-in observational callback before text input is processed.

Studio owns script undo history because ImGui's native undo buffer cannot hold
large Replace All edits. Undo needs the caret and selection after pointer input
but before deletion, paste or typing. Existing callbacks do not expose that
point. This callback reports the live offsets without changing input ordering.

The patch applies to the pinned ImGui source through scripts/vendor-tree.sh.
When ImGui changes its text-input implementation, recheck the callback placement
against pointer selection, text, keyboard and clipboard handling before rebasing.

--- a/imgui.h
+++ b/imgui.h
@@ -1370,6 +1370,7 @@
     ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackCharFilter  = 1 << 21,  // Callback on character inputs to replace or discard them. Modify 'EventChar' to replace or discard, or return 1 in callback to discard.
     ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackResize      = 1 << 22,  // Callback on buffer capacity changes request (beyond 'buf_size' parameter value), allowing the string to grow. Notify when the string wants to be resized (for string types which hold a cache of their Size). You will be provided a new BufSize in the callback and NEED to honor it. (see misc/cpp/imgui_stdlib.h for an example of using this)
     ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackEdit        = 1 << 23,  // Callback on any edit. Note that InputText() already returns true on edit + you can always use IsItemEdited(). The callback is useful to manipulate the underlying buffer while focus is active.
+    ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackBeforeInput = 1 << 29,  // Observe caret and selection after pointer handling and before text or key input.
 
     // Multi-line Word-Wrapping [BETA]
     // - Not well tested yet. Please report any incorrect cursor movement, selection behavior etc. bug to https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/issues/3237.
--- a/imgui_widgets.cpp
+++ b/imgui_widgets.cpp
@@ -5162,6 +5162,20 @@
         if (state->SelectedAllMouseLock && !io.MouseDown[0])
             state->SelectedAllMouseLock = false;
 
+        if ((flags & ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackBeforeInput) && callback)
+        {
+            ImGuiInputTextCallbackData callback_data;
+            callback_data.Ctx = &g;
+            callback_data.ID = state->ID;
+            callback_data.Flags = flags;
+            callback_data.EventFlag = ImGuiInputTextFlags_CallbackBeforeInput;
+            callback_data.CursorPos = state->Stb->cursor;
+            callback_data.SelectionStart = state->Stb->select_start;
+            callback_data.SelectionEnd = state->Stb->select_end;
+            callback_data.UserData = callback_user_data;
+            callback(&callback_data);
+        }
+
